Sval: Linux desktop integration names Sval by its own application id

Gecko registers with the desktop portal as org.mozilla.firefox whatever the
application's identity (DoRegisterHostApp), and the portal's permission
store keys its grants by that id, so Sval and an installed Firefox shared
their notification, location, camera, screen sharing and background grants.
Sval registers app.sval.sval, the distribution id followed by the remoting
name, which is also the name of its desktop entry. Notifications and MPRIS
name the same desktop entry, so the desktop finds Sval's name and icon for
them.

The remoting name stays sval: it is the program name the windows carry,
and the desktop entry's StartupWMClass ties those windows to the entry.

